CM_ "ADAS vehicle bus. 500 kbit/s, 11-bit identifiers, little-endian (Intel) signal layout throughout. Identifier order IS priority order: sensor object lists (0x100) outrank the driver command (0x200) so a sensor veto is never delayed by operator input. THREE nodes: gateway, vehicle control, and one front sensor node carrying a four-element VL53L0X array. Identifiers 0x110 (SensorSide_Object), 0x111 (SensorSide_Raw), 0x703 (SS_Heartbeat) and NodeAddress 4 are RESERVED for a side sensor node - held free so adding one later needs no renumbering.";
CM_ BU_ GW "Gateway node, STM32F103. Bridges the 2.4 GHz operator link to the vehicle bus. Publishes driver intent, consumes vehicle status for telemetry.";
CM_ BU_ VC "Vehicle control node, STM32F103. Consumes object lists and driver intent, arbitrates per axis, runs AEB, drives the TB6612 and reads the encoders.";
CM_ BU_ SF "Front sensor node, STM32F103. VL53L0X time-of-flight array, tracking done locally.";
CM_ BO_ 256 "Front fused object - the closest in-path object across every sensor on the node. THE AEB INPUT PATH, and the only sensor message the vehicle-control node needs to act. Event-triggered: transmitted whenever any sensor produces a new measurement, so ~13 ms with four sensors on a 50 ms timing budget. GenMsgCycleTime is a watchdog maximum, not a promise.";
CM_ BO_ 257 "Front per-sensor raw ranges, round-robin. Sensors measure concurrently on a 50 ms budget; one sensor is transmitted per slot, so every index refreshes within 50 ms. Diagnostics and the wider situational picture - NOT the AEB path. Deliberately lower priority than 0x100.";
CM_ BO_ 512 "Driver intent, a byte-for-byte translation of the RF control frame in contracts/rf_protocol.h. The gateway performs no interpretation.";
CM_ BO_ 768 "Vehicle control state, faults, and what was actually applied to the actuators. Cycle 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 784 "Measured vehicle motion plus the AEB last-point-to-brake distance. Cycle 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1792 "Gateway liveness. Cycle 100 ms. Absence for 300 ms is a node-loss fault.";
CM_ BO_ 1793 "Vehicle control liveness. Cycle 100 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1794 "Front sensor liveness. Cycle 100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_E2eCrc "AUTOSAR E2E Profile 1 style CRC-8 (poly 0x1D) over the CAN identifier used as Data ID, then payload bytes 1..7.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_E2eAlv "Alive counter, increments modulo 16 each transmission. The receiver rejects a repeated or skipped value.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_Range "Distance to the closest in-path object. 0 is only valid when SF_Status is NO_TARGET.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_RangeRate "Signed range rate. NEGATIVE means closing - this is the sign convention AEB depends on.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_TrackAge "Consecutive cycles this track has been associated. AEB requires a minimum age before it will act.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_Confidence "Monotonic 0..63 quality score. Not a percentage.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_ObjCount "How many sensors on this node currently report a valid in-path target. 0 means the fused fields carry no object.";
CM_ SG_ 256 SF_SampleAge "Age of the underlying measurement when this frame was transmitted, in 20 ms steps. Event-triggered transmission should keep this at 0; a persistently non-zero value means the node is publishing faster than it is measuring, and the receiver is seeing repeats.";
CM_ SG_ 257 SFR_SensorIdx "Which physical sensor this frame describes, 0..N-1 in the node's own wiring-table order. The layout is identical for every index, so this is a plain field rather than a DBC multiplexor.";
CM_ SG_ 257 SFR_SlotAge "Milliseconds between this sensor's measurement completing and this frame being transmitted. Near zero when the measurement starts are staggered to match the transmit slots; large values mean the stagger has drifted and readings are going out stale.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GW_Steering "Mirrors rf_control_frame_t.steering, -100 full left to +100 full right.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GW_LinkOk "Cleared when the RF failsafe timeout (150 ms) has expired. The command fields are zeroed at the same time, so a stale command cannot be acted upon.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GW_RfSeq "Mirrors the RF frame sequence number, carried onto CAN so end-to-end latency can be measured from one trace.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GW_FrameAge "Milliseconds between RF reception and CAN transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GW_LinkQuality "Valid RF frames received in the last 16 expected slots.";
CM_ SG_ 768 VC_Faults "Bitfield: 0 CAN bus-off, 1 front sensor timeout, 2 RESERVED (side sensor timeout - no side node in the three-MCU build), 3 gateway timeout, 4 E2E failure, 5 motor fault, 6 encoder fault, 7 clock fault.";
CM_ SG_ 768 VC_E2eErrCount "Saturating count of E2E rejections since reset. Non-zero is a bus integrity problem, not a transient.";
CM_ SG_ 784 VCM_Speed "Longitudinal speed from the wheel encoders. Positive is forward.";
CM_ SG_ 784 VCM_LpbDistance "Last-point-to-brake distance the AEB currently computes for the measured speed. Published so the ten-run validation protocol can be scored from a bus trace alone.";


